From 083742142e21fb01b8b1d564d9f1380adc0e0bd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:54:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] layer_panel: A drag's end cancels the surface's implicit grab
 of the press.

The press on the Dock's (or the Clip's) surface started the surface's
implicit grab; the release went to the drag (a launcher dropped, or the
Dock moved), never to the surface. The grab stayed: the panel then took
any motion, and the next click anywhere went to it while the seat's
pointer focus was elsewhere (the assertion of surface.c, 0178). Lab
scenario: 4 of 5 runs had such a click before, 0 of 5 now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/layer_panel.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/layer_panel.c b/src/layer_panel.c
index 9f08bc4..083a910 100644
--- a/src/layer_panel.c
+++ b/src/layer_panel.c
@@ -1474,6 +1474,14 @@ void _wlmaker_layer_panel_end_drag(wlmaker_layer_panel_t *layer_panel_ptr)
         wlmtk_container_pointer_grab_release(
             element_ptr->parent_container_ptr, element_ptr);
     }
+    // The surface's own grab, from the button press: The release went to
+    // the drag, never to the surface. Left, it kept the pointer on the panel
+    // (any motion "accepted"), so the next click anywhere went to this
+    // panel while the seat's focus was elsewhere.
+    if (NULL != layer_panel_ptr->super_panel.super_container.
+        pointer_grab_element_ptr) {
+        layer_panel_ptr->orig_element_vmt.pointer_grab_cancel(element_ptr);
+    }
 }
 
